{"id": "tea:sankaradigvijaya:11", "source": "src:sankaradigvijaya", "location": {"ref": "11"}, "paraphrase": "At Śrīśaila the Kāpālika Ugrabhairava asks Śaṅkara for his head as an offering to win Bhairava's favour; Śaṅkara consents, but his disciple Padmapāda, possessed by Narasiṃha, kills the Kāpālika.", "tags": {"level": "unmarked", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "unmarked"}, "types": ["dispute", "teacher-transmission"], "disputes": ["dsp:kapalika-path-validity"], "teachers": ["tch:sankara", "tch:padmapada"], "reported_by_opponent": true, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U17-pasupata-kapalika"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "notes": "Opponent's / outsider's report: Mādhavīya Śaṅkaradigvijaya, Advaita hagiography hostile to the Kāpālikas. Canto number from memory.", "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U17-pasupata-kapalika"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
