{"id": "tea:sankaradigvijaya:5", "source": "src:sankaradigvijaya", "location": {"ref": "5"}, "paraphrase": "The tradition's account: as a boy Śaṅkara, seized by a crocodile, obtained his mother's permission to renounce, promised to return at her death, and went north to Govinda on the Narmadā, who initiated him.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "teachers": ["tch:sankara", "tch:govinda-bhagavatpada"], "notes": "Tradition's account; canto low confidence.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U13-advaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U13-advaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:sankaradigvijaya:8-10", "source": "src:sankaradigvijaya", "location": {"ref": "8-10"}, "paraphrase": "The tradition's account: at Māhiṣmatī Śaṅkara debated Maṇḍana Miśra, champion of Vedic ritual, on whether knowledge or works liberates, with Ubhaya Bhāratī as judge; she declared Śaṅkara the victor when Maṇḍana's garland faded first, and Maṇḍana became Śaṅkara's disciple Sureśvara.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "action"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission", "dispute"], "teachers": ["tch:sankara", "tch:mandana-misra", "tch:ubhaya-bharati"], "disputes": ["dsp:works-knowledge-grace", "dsp:jnana-karma-samuccaya"], "notes": "Tradition's account (hagiography); canto numbers low confidence.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U13-advaita"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U13-advaita"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
